0ce869e005" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d94dadb2-4fe3-5787-929d-74b940cbadc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110597" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2ed737550ddf5502d2a066cdc279285b624000a6c2ad8464496c122ad31a3ab.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But, \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad39641-56c0-508c-9b90-0cc2e2767b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461641} {:answer/id #uuid "02252817-c38b-5820-b87f-ed1696a4c751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ad39641-56c0-508c-9b90-0cc2e2767b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461641} :answer-field/id #uuid "857885bf-7367-5e75-8ec5-43d94868cb82" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73f09b04-09ec-5e1f-bdf5-e3178c28f434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461643} {:answer/id #uuid "01faef8b-4f0b-51b2-80ff-1f9d1ade44d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73f09b04-09ec-5e1f-bdf5-e3178c28f434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461643} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d5341b-98e6-512b-8142-c17dfa8068d4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c52a9d4d-a545-519c-8a5a-0c045175f03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461645} {:answer/id #uuid "15b5b644-7d14-50d4-8d39-f862963ee03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c52a9d4d-a545-519c-8a5a-0c045175f03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461645} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac97ed8-0d07-5bff-b5b5-97985053e7bd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f37be5a-fb02-59a0-9bc3-1e609a53d6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110600" :question/problem "![](images/81/815f5ce1dd5bf3bc30b7853b53cd97736ffeb8224f30bc864cc7e43e07bedb5a.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1094661c-8c7c-5f85-b731-4dadb0aec310" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Using Set Notation Are Subspaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea812525-5990-52cf-b86e-78f1b4de8995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461647} {:answer/id #uuid "8f213eb6-2142-5889-90e4-c372925d0dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea812525-5990-52cf-b86e-78f1b4de8995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461647} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9799888-3637-5f54-acd6-ed3396e155dd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af6b52c-a109-53f6-aa27-67a8c43708cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461649} {:answer/id #uuid "ff863854-8a24-5221-be5f-d347d25b3c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff863854-8a24-5221-be5f-d347d25b3c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461650} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c50586-e18a-5fca-a9fa-4b003d93b2c7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f70460d9-df3a-58dd-95a2-bafff6dc83d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461651} {:answer/id #uuid "61868caa-f76b-5288-8ca4-5d353e006f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f70460d9-df3a-58dd-95a2-bafff6dc83d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461651} :answer-field/id #uuid "18092fb5-74d5-5ff7-870d-5e5eab99935e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d55fbe8-7170-5840-8a9a-b1f2a55c58fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-110611" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n- **I.** $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=1}$\n- **II.** $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x+y-z=0}$\n- **III.** $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $xyz=1$ since $0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x+y-z=0$ since $0+0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1094661c-8c7c-5f85-b731-4dadb0aec310" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Using Set Notation Are Subspaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba35c72-4811-55d0-b2b1-fb8116a2cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461653} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2a422a-84a1-5671-bc55-3b45224e58cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ba35c72-4811-55d0-b2b1-fb8116a2cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461653} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0888cfa-5fff-5bcc-9c6f-d3cf0a398b99" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2974aa62-0b1f-5343-a4a5-c39a1584c078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461655} {:answer/id #uuid "78c8ebf0-1d54-5046-ae1c-3426546d3565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c8ebf0-1d54-5046-ae1c-3426546d3565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461656} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad91d256-6b2d-51b9-8149-c46bca013503" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5784de9d-74b4-5c34-9c61-2b2f1a7172ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461657} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa10535-80e6-5c1d-a5e9-5bed7b7ca613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5784de9d-74b4-5c34-9c61-2b2f1a7172ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461657} :answer-field/id #uuid "822bc400-c192-58d1-80df-f14e9a428a6a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49bd226a-4547-5889-a62c-e6c2912a1520" :question/math-academy-id "q-110760" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x-4y=1\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0\\}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each subset.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. For instance, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x-4y=1$ since $0-4\\cdot 0=0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=-2y$ since $0=-2\\cdot 0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. No point in ${R}^{3}$ satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0.$ Hence, $C=∅.$ The empty set is not a subspace since it does not contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1094661c-8c7c-5f85-b731-4dadb0aec310" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Using Set Notation Are Subspaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6d33351-e47b-5dcf-8a4d-d3e61f058c5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461659} {:answer/id #uuid "d95202b2-7ac0-51a9-beba-433590fd067c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d33351-e47b-5dcf-8a4d-d3e61f058c5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461659} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7a303b-9974-55fa-9193-b45a893b05b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c0fe0f-a14e-5a97-bb81-d2b618017a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461661} {:answer/id #uuid "52cb8444-2346-56eb-8483-17ca5a3815c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52cb8444-2346-56eb-8483-17ca5a3815c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461662} :answer-field/id #uuid "df43bab4-a790-5959-8eef-b12b9e48205b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c438405c-079c-5cda-acfc-5fc8f4718e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461663} {:answer/id #uuid "688e99c6-1ace-56a4-a978-0e19e70df677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c438405c-079c-5cda-acfc-5fc8f4718e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461663} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fcae7ac-a05d-5215-8944-c0e4000c37c6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc11ea3b-3ee9-5cb9-a26d-3aab9cb82498" :question/math-academy-id "q-110761" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n- **I.** $A={⟨2t,2+t⟩\\,:\\,t\\in R}$\n- **II.** $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0}$\n- **III.** $C={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:y=1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. If the origin belongs to this subset, we would have, for some $t$:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 2+t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives us\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t=0 \\\\ 2+t=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the system has no solution. So, $0$ is not in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace.  It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x-y=0$ since $0-0=0.$ So, $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $y=1$ since $0\\ne 1.$ So, $0$ is not in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6faebac8-ebda-5f28-9ae5-f47ea62ba4d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461665} {:answer/id #uuid "89f5755d-41a2-5951-8169-455f39e871ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89f5755d-41a2-5951-8169-455f39e871ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461666} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f6caba-9c1c-5b6e-b1e1-a94766e26a33" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a776ef48-bad8-5973-b3d2-424cd31a8efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461667} {:answer/id #uuid "03cb7ee7-1cb7-5269-9d2c-bcb3d98685e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a776ef48-bad8-5973-b3d2-424cd31a8efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461667} :answer-field/id #uuid "b94d55a2-ccc3-50de-94dc-85a31579f29d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71e6b7db-27af-50cb-9f24-3efd638462db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461669} {:answer/id #uuid "638eb8bc-d919-5679-86a7-346c5b27b82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "638eb8bc-d919-5679-86a7-346c5b27b82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461670} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b59df70-0a5b-5c66-b162-e3a8bbcf21c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57caf7d5-ab2c-51c1-a72f-c7af8b4259a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-112114" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b46093feaf5d7138e30c6d6fc673a2d915cac74a23ae76e0841e9bb5b135fa60.png)\n\nThe graph of the polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The degree of $P(x)$ is even.\n- The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n- The constant term is positive.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nSo, statement I is true, while statement II is false.\n\nLastly, note that the $y$-intercept is positive, and therefore the constant term must be positive. So, III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68350e0d-84ca-5b50-b05a-1bca3ceea40f" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 3x3 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f56d4881-7927-5529-b7ce-6e102c93f448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461671} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9dce1c-b833-5c08-93d1-0c74dc942a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f56d4881-7927-5529-b7ce-6e102c93f448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461671} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4cde7f3-5f67-5b5b-9c7a-6d7bf978beb9" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cee9a4a5-d913-56a8-83f1-b7f62e66a405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461673} {:answer/id #uuid "86853822-71a9-5acb-bb33-07c7ce5b8214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #e