$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-\\pi /8}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{{x}^{4}+2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}+2}{3}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\frac{(-x)^{4}+2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}+2}{3} \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & ={e}^{-x}-{e}^{-(-x)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-h(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5308fdae-66ac-55f0-b4da-27db3ce4f77b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461731} {:answer/id #uuid "2dba8359-29a8-5c41-9ce0-8cd798fe3188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dba8359-29a8-5c41-9ce0-8cd798fe3188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5488a179-9079-59d7-9085-615f460e3a6a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d54e93db-9c96-5419-b787-d23233125885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461733} {:answer/id #uuid "3f036de2-329a-5c05-8a56-59d7cf3f3ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d54e93db-9c96-5419-b787-d23233125885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461733} :answer-field/id #uuid "aab98f01-e316-525e-9035-202a3d8e921d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462620} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73e30afc-d20e-5512-ba6d-f275ac7bcd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461735} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6a8841-0712-5636-aeca-0549d0f059b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73e30afc-d20e-5512-ba6d-f275ac7bcd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461735} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6025f86-40f6-5cdc-a65f-78f6bb489b93" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd35b4dd-cb0b-59b9-9a08-35fd436a6a59" :question/math-academy-id "q-115278" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{1+2{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\sqrt[3]{-x} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)=\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{1+2{x}^{4}}$ is an odd function, but integral III is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13445-0218-5950-967e-a68bcfec32c7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66d0ae76-bc3f-5fc2-ab45-3c327cc7dc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461737} {:answer/id #uuid "cf878234-afe8-5395-85e8-d9b0f6944666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66d0ae76-bc3f-5fc2-ab45-3c327cc7dc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461737} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db57aa6-14c2-54c7-b692-04ab1d30d57d" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5768034-5162-5525-968a-d216e70073e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461739} {:answer/id #uuid "d62d551d-96da-517f-8340-2d16b1ab916d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d62d551d-96da-517f-8340-2d16b1ab916d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461740} :answer-field/id #uuid "15477831-2eef-57fc-a8a7-8d7564cd6fcf" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a0b5c9f-f227-5d04-9202-326caee8424f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461741} {:answer/id #uuid "a3404bbe-548f-5c40-9fdc-310af0e7676b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3404bbe-548f-5c40-9fdc-310af0e7676b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461742} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fc2c1ee-5fd8-59cf-97ff-a46de525b2f3" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4dac05e-84dd-5a26-905f-fb4d126dc4c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11556" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 0.5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1.5 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $P$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $3$ rows and $2$ columns, so it's a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $S$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $T$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $5$ rows and $5$ columns, so it is a $5\\times 5$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $S$ and $T$ are square matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ede6800b-ecfd-5ef8-a386-4aec94ddd89c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6994d8c9-98b2-50b8-8431-920fc2e5ca2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461743} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7ed713-7032-5945-903d-d1bdd3f2120f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f7ed713-7032-5945-903d-d1bdd3f2120f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461744} :answer-field/id #uuid "d421249e-95dd-51d3-a30d-7cb392461860" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462625} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0524a498-8b2b-59fb-b65e-ad0ec383d4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461745} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0e7187-d6c3-5198-b64c-9805c15ccdc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0524a498-8b2b-59fb-b65e-ad0ec383d4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461745} :answer-field/id #uuid "731022f7-d0bc-5408-8e58-15a92c89fc00" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462626} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aeb0246-e841-5d68-8e79-25722b8f2690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461747} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f043b3-1b23-50d2-be97-efc89a8fde6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aeb0246-e841-5d68-8e79-25722b8f2690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461747} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddc36ee2-30f9-5080-926a-4269f7f8d44b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1598c957-f6d6-5194-a4fb-4b15b46e8010" :question/math-academy-id "q-115716" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a0b39135b78cefe8471c7d120850dde9b53786342679b5ed7f25af9110350607.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=-x(x-3)$\n- ${y}^{′}=9-{x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(x-2)(x-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/a4/a43217f2af81c1bbacbebd8800b7ebcd4076a32d6ff61782e1fdab4cd182d5ee.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $x=3,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-x(x-3)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=9-{x}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not evaluate to zero at both $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x(x-2)(x-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=3,$ but it also evaluates to zero when $x=2,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ede6800b-ecfd-5ef8-a386-4aec94ddd89c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "599a2f16-4cde-5b11-988c-26ef6ae958a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461749} {:answer/id #uuid "674e2162-0aff-5e89-ad5d-62f1b7b88b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "674e2162-0aff-5e89-ad5d-62f1b7b88b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461750} :answer-field/id #uuid "20ff9988-96ed-5003-87b8-1e50061b9644" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be3027b6-c98a-5856-aca0-5295856401ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461751} {:answer/id #uuid "6c01d811-543d-5cfd-a487-a2c4a796ed80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be3027b6-c98a-5856-aca0-5295856401ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461751} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c26860d-fdb0-5342-ba78-a18246e190b7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9d9fed-e7f0-5b89-861f-08c01e74a252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461753} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd923e9-73f9-5490-93f0-f510865e93b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9d9fed-e7f0-5b89-861f-08c01e74a252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461753} :answer-field/id #uuid "871cff07-5ca0-53fe-88a4-54bbc09aa803" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c861b6c2-4257-5ae6-8d33-89c2fd430076" :question/math-academy-id "q-115719" :question/problem "![](images/17/170ddea2148f369d4feedd14540f234d7946bb6670d1ca6eb4c4ebbbb086a760.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+7)$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(x+3)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+5)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/cf/cf77e09457cd6b53da801a6eb876a79712935eba623c851a5b6dafa58887a076.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=-7,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+7)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-7$ and $x=-3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x(x+3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not evaluate to zero at $x=-7,$ and also evaluates to zero when $x=0,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+5)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ but it also evaluates to zero when $x=-5,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32b9a92b-880b-50de-b8e9-648fa219b83f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88fc7cc8-79d5-59d3-ad2c-04b64b84f0ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461755} {:answer/id #uuid "6262e720-b181-540c-bdb0-37bb9b9572a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88fc7cc8-79d5-59d3-ad2c-04b64b84f0ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461755} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9f91efd-4f5f-59b4-b78b-62d93d7a34fd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8590a88d-c93e-5cb6-834a-cd06d60f91f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461757} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2dccd5-90a7-5939-a2f3-ba68c00652df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b2dccd5-90a7-5939-a2f3-ba68c00652df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461758} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d29f83-bdb4-5fcd-8a8c-93e6a7035123" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462632} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80541672-0915-5b6c-9017-9ac341bd9f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461759} {:answer/id #uuid "a2defdda-9879-5425-b8f7-043e2815e940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80541672-0915-5b6c-9017-9ac341bd9f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461759} :answer-field/id #uuid "77bf2e3a-fe25-597e-9fd5-53baa9f801cd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "988f2d4b-1d26-5c62-baed-2061d6f81ef4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115751" :question/problem "![](images/25/2552222c6a0be1b1bf1e67a66b4906bb735c2d974d724d3e25e988d15388c696.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{8}{x+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/eb/eb1303132a4fe6a26c85b4733a3039a52109b4c49408e1c82038d71885d27f70.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-1.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side approaches $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -1,$ but it also approaches $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to 1,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{8}{x+1}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{8}{x+1}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}=-\\frac{x}{(1+\\frac{1}{x})}\\to ∓\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32b9a92b-880b-50de-b8e9-648fa219b83f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0181da5-8614-58af-ac14-1a9336d4dbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461761} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2eec4c-4f47-514b-bf5d-f2c38895ac0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0181da5-8614-58af-ac14-1a9336d4dbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461761} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc6800d-212e-50df-85f3-d5b35178961d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84b32df7-b0d9-5ac9-b15a-2fa4213ca142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461763} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4b5a3f-874e-5bd2-a618-5e76d2280ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84b32df7-b0d9-5ac9-b15a-2fa4213ca142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461763} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bef5e3b-3082-5dd7-8c06-9ea6d0a08d4c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462635} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0de8a2f-f221-5129-bf2e-e14033c84895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461765} {:answer/id #uuid "61d491ae-9078-571e-8681-ef4d10f41b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61d491ae-9078-571e-8681-ef4d10f41b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461766} :answer-field/id #uuid "61918825-a1f6-5a04-9d13-9a6f5063d1ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3be4e44a-f534-5d30-81ef-fc22fbf18076" :question/math-academy-id "q-115754" :question/problem "![](images/34/34af8d1078100aea331c300ea529d2fdefbdd31e99ee8a7946325d58a8abf680.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=7-{x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/d0/d02883b776dbcd55c5c96347ed1a7bb0e51ef8c26e62786049b6585b878d04fb.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-7.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=7-{x}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not approach $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -7.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x+7}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(1+\\frac{7}{x})}\\to -\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{x+7}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "762c5225-00bd-5d2f-9859-394f886482cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05bfcbaa-d2b1-5fe0-ad56-ec1eaae881ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461767} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f5ed1e-509a-5016-b984-67ee16a92bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05bfcbaa-d2b1-5fe0-ad56-ec1eaae881ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461767} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0bff3c9-f537-55cb-a1c9-27fc825821aa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73346110-21be-5682-8e62-0adb727d81ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461769} {:answer/id #uuid "26e67922-9884-5bea-aa66-b917a449fbbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26e67922-9884-5bea-aa66-b917a449fbbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461770} :answer-field/id #uuid "92a7748a-62c0-5f15-97d3-4cfba9d041af" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3782d80d-50d4-5d80-8925-6ddad28cab0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461771} {:answer/id #uuid "f789845b-9090-5a1d-b191-815a29e6ff58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3782d80d-50d4-5d80-8925-6ddad28cab0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461771} :answer-field/id #uuid "517e6b35-18b0-5548-9e90-b787cba99ee2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ef86548-9209-58c6-a39c-c5582ffe1c99" :question/math-academy-id "q-115813" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a2a2b4b141f4f0c250e4865b174b9eb32b1ed4ab94cc6ebd074131673d5712c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=-2{x}^{2}-4x-2$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2x+1$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}-1$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "![](images/69/69465ce0573d7b6deac631663766a5dd1c90afa29eeb0c5286cb5ef1f7ee1153.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the line $x=-1.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on this line.\n\n- Second, the line $x=-1$ divides the plane into $2$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $2$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2{x}^{2}-4x-2=-2(x+1)^{2}\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2x+1=(x+1)^{2}\n$$\n\ngives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-1=(x+1)(x-1)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "954f8004-35b4-58ec-be26-2beccfd5f8e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Equilibrium Solutions"}] :question/an