-ac52-5561-ac65-e3710790558e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a309c64-ac52-5561-ac65-e3710790558e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461850} :answer-field/id #uuid "df96a148-3ab6-53a8-bfb3-0111bf03f0d5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bfbb710f-9bcf-5482-b898-5f45cf7ceff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-117366" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- **II.** $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\n- **III.** $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110588 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f045b43-4785-5989-8b5a-dcb8401d1bb3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Graph of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c78a2d78-de5b-55db-9598-b2738d47cf1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461851} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2cfab7-7117-5fc2-99af-f66e7b541971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b2cfab7-7117-5fc2-99af-f66e7b541971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461852} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58d20dc-9c7d-500c-a86a-f3f1271fa49f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94823d85-e3b3-52c9-9f56-e5542e922a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461853} {:answer/id #uuid "24ead7ad-8485-5ded-ae26-9d6c7d203b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94823d85-e3b3-52c9-9f56-e5542e922a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461853} :answer-field/id #uuid "809ec92f-116c-5ca0-acee-614fc750aad8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8e8f20-54be-52d5-9909-13466cd4de2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461855} {:answer/id #uuid "f79a093b-71bd-5e31-bb2f-d45dcebd2e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f79a093b-71bd-5e31-bb2f-d45dcebd2e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461856} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fce65dd-a328-5462-9d11-7b16710dbaba" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d01f8dbc-d72d-57bf-bd1d-25c6d02854e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-117371" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n- **II.** $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3})$\n- **III.** $(0,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{7\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{7\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(0,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,0)$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172017 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1616167b-5679-5ff6-b385-3e1b59352c64" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c63043b-4d95-5271-bd03-04c48cf42652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461857} {:answer/id #uuid "c435a8df-48c3-55f3-bf34-545dd961babb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c63043b-4d95-5271-bd03-04c48cf42652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461857} :answer-field/id #uuid "69e6dd76-17e5-5d00-b6a3-2725217da17c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f3b0f15-11c5-5f91-8e39-a4700396d70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461859} {:answer/id #uuid "413ccddf-0828-5899-b41a-c5b854115744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f3b0f15-11c5-5f91-8e39-a4700396d70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461859} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8bbbbd-3619-58c4-a2c4-e30a857f4e01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa9e1a21-a120-5fbf-b91e-9951a669f7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461861} {:answer/id #uuid "5bfa0a89-a5fb-5b03-9b6b-0a15e263c8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bfa0a89-a5fb-5b03-9b6b-0a15e263c8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461862} :answer-field/id #uuid "569a9252-47cd-5e75-9c9f-40b194a881a6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f47e52f5-b113-5140-ac0d-d3912c7ac7a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-118025" :question/problem "![](images/50/5077a94fe8b5d5435b5bf50d0ea687f5bc87ae95011e22800ccfe473f8af78dd.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=xy-x$\n- ${y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}+2xy+x$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "![](images/2f/2f7075161363dee2817aeb8aff9e85781a10bd30c926bfff73724992eee699ac.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $y=-1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=0$ and $y=-1$ divide the plane into $4$ quarters. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ quarters are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>-1$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation I does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}={x}^{2}(y+1)\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=xy-x=x(y-1)\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=1.$\n\n- Equation III gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}+2xy+x=x(y+1)^{2}\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14f1707a-a6cd-5d59-84fa-27f9eeb71ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461863} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba76389-92e4-5ccf-8712-d8fd82870166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f1707a-a6cd-5d59-84fa-27f9eeb71ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461863} :answer-field/id #uuid "7aa4482b-dc1b-5133-8c44-f7dca0376eaa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c30e83-48fb-55db-8c1e-f667f6d945ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461865} {:answer/id #uuid "ea94a37b-3120-54ff-b365-49b1f70de0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea94a37b-3120-54ff-b365-49b1f70de0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461866} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e94ea8d-e75e-58b7-909a-2691939879a2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f16e010-7de1-5279-964b-71ac44e40c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461867} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3a1e30-5262-5347-b264-bd971063a0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f16e010-7de1-5279-964b-71ac44e40c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461867} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0f26be7-fb2b-5772-81c1-0d6c2abc0164" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41da8ad0-e0fc-5f39-8eb7-c4706c551e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-118976" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dcd36221e7ad293f0aac1ab99ece80641cb077efd05adc168a552e97d86100c8.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\nI. $\\overset{\\to }{AD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n\nII. $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{FA}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Equality I is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}.$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{FA}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "932fd48b-8935-57c7-8293-eb9a71377d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461869} {:answer/id #uuid "56de3e7c-351f-5781-a84d-24f381e2d6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56de3e7c-351f-5781-a84d-24f381e2d6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461870} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf424628-63d2-57e6-be5d-101e46f767e7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a3ca570-83fb-5da6-a3be-00fe526ae7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461871} {:answer/id #uuid "d7703abf-77ac-5af8-a67c-13948de7e60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7703abf-77ac-5af8-a67c-13948de7e60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461872} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15d3225-3000-55f2-ab15-7cd57eec9d48" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f70e53bd-3eda-5218-a9f5-043d667b741e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461873} {:answer/id #uuid "aed5fbc2-44e7-5a80-8887-c43bc5e676bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aed5fbc2-44e7-5a80-8887-c43bc5e676bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461874} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d3e201f-dd08-57df-b785-f1e323a09839" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3510664b-2f53-5d5d-9a15-f28784a8e0c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11961" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,-3),(0,5),(2,-5).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(3,-2)$\n- **II.** $(-5,0)$\n- **III.** $(5,2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,-2),(-5,0),(5,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092346 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2371a64-5e91-5caa-91c0-f6c7ff572c70" :knowledge-point/title "Rotating an Object About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d2902e-fe58-53b7-9bea-3127e6359fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461875} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac292f-81f0-5439-8f10-2af989375112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac292f-81f0-5439-8f10-2af989375112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461876} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eb618ec-27a1-5c30-9f69-da8678e0d24e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a721534-6ddd-57ca-b5b5-8ac253bdf5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461877} {:answer/id #uuid "022bbf55-1062-54d5-aec8-1dd458f8a82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a721534-6ddd-57ca-b5b5-8ac253bdf5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461877} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c8256e-8dfb-5fb9-b88c-844f3965001a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e47ca5-94e2-5e80-99e4-0cf645a6be09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461879} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff35a1a-1e27-5a4c-99ed-19f6834bf2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68e47ca5-94e2-5e80-99e4-0cf645a6be09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461879} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b6b0bfd-1f1e-5700-8876-61f888ab4569" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34508741-6c7f-54ff-a124-34cef40dd55c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11967" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(-1,2),(2,-3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under a **clockwise** rotation of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(0,\\sqrt{2})$\n- **II.** $(3,-1)$\n- **III.** $(-5,1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\theta =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into the above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the transformation, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the rotation $R$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{ }[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are \n\n$$\n(0,\\sqrt{2}),\\,(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,(-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}).\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f05073e6-bfb4-5b8d-8db4-310e7dfa5a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461881} {:answer/id #uuid "f8cc566f-6c98-5ea4-b7be-dc39ac81a01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f05073e6-bfb4-5b8d-8db4-310e7dfa5a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461881} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5f69b8e-f7c4-5e0a-9f1d-00394a46cc6a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04970681-2afb-550f-9388-bd0cba68f0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461883} {:answer/id #uuid "2edff474-152a-55c0-91ad-ecc28535f220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04970681-2afb-550f-9388-bd0cba68f0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461883} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa044452-e56e-5ba8-a718-24f5a020ad8c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5254f4e8-74dd-5cce-a282-1148360c51fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461885} {:answer/id #uuid "f5978d27-0a47-584a-877f-15e8629c4892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5978d27-0a47-584a-877f-15e8629c4892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461886} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdc29db2-90c6-5990-862a-26c63df63336" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d13de60-db83-5fa3-ae76-e5805b3d5848" :question/math-academy-id "q-11974" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,-2),(-3,2),(2,2),$ and $(-1,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n- **I.** $(2,2)$\n- **II.** $(0,1)$\n- **III.** $(-5,-8)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-(-2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(0,-2),(-5,-8),(0,2),(0,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ede6800b-ecfd-5ef8-a386-4aec94ddd89c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ff08fd4-e76a-5634-bb6e-0c9a6b0b3993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461887} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdb674f-ffd4-54b9-8c1e-4f91a2dc3f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ff08fd4-e76a-5634-bb6e-0c9a6b0b3993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461887} :answer-field/id #uuid "82e63362-cab2-5e7e-83e8-f22d22398220" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e608e253-42d4-5961-8843-52ddbcf614d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461889} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0fdb5-8f4c-57c8-a23f-45439729d652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0fdb5-8f4c-57c8-a23f-45439729d652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461890} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0864e24-ac68-556b-ac40-cfab9960b432" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbff8f6c-be50-5006-8ae5-e8ea53b23903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461891} {:answer/id #uuid "6120c7e4-6551-59ac-890c-ed12d399ae95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbff8f6c-be50-5006-8ae5-e8ea53b23903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461891} :answer-field/id #uuid "90e05925-1a87-58ef-9da7-8a4d05b06a6d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf3614e8-6b2e-5b66-a1c3-8c10682d44be" :question/math-academy-id "q-120025" :question/problem "![](images/17/17cd72acbe8dd412d37c51ff992278d9664f6c5b1141a8604278fda76e57700f.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=x-2$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x-2)$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(x+1)(x-2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/5d/5d6165488c8e41c16cf31b1b000a924344399c2b94a8fe5e7138c55adf97602b.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $x=2,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x-2$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not evaluate to zero at both $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x-2)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x(x+1)(x-2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=2,$ but it also evaluates to zero when $x=-1,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5277f56d-3f2d-505c-bf73-48207a2310a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982cc208-4ef7-53b6-b14e-eddf19d4f7f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461893} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4796b3-871f-5f81-a235-937da5930fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc4796b3-871f-5f81-a235-937da5930fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461894} :answer-field/id #uuid "313eb125-e9e4-5cbd-b384-ea16df717365" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc9b1942-b0bc-54f8-a6c3-1ff051b6a113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461895} {:answer/id #uuid "e858c129-3cbe-507d-9eca-9bb753521056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc9b1942-b0bc-54f8-a6c3-1ff051b6a113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461895} :answer-field/id #uuid "da434888-6e69-5683-b144-41c6022c0ca0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2191303c-5047-5ef5-8284-5beaca1777ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461897} {:answer/id #uuid "6eab0a1c-68e9-523d-9519-74a67c6d7470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2191303c-5047-5ef5-8284-5beaca1777ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461897} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf290901-b724-5bf9-b2cb-39afaae04ac0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a07799d5-cf00-5be4-9950-028a4e658d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120038" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f855062048a7d38b2fa6c843701a182661b2235b2042ad83fbedd600b1dd770c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "![](images/8f/8fdec9bda9e2bcc514e56a14a6608b2f0cb74fd0943a51c944b29cc047e02cd9.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$ gives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=2,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "762c5225-00bd-5d2f-9859-394f886482cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "278ae8de-7b07-5a39-bd04-2bf57e898f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461899} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e575c9-1a51-597f-84b4-2c9662352a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8e575c9-1a51-597f-84b4-2c9662352a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461900} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a25f6e5-8bae-5e17-a73e-a1406b38edcd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16036a91-f98e-56f8-b955-49aab5c89324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461901} {:answer/id #uuid "66df9c9a-852d-5e75-85f8-abb65b295796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16036a91-f98e-56f8-b955-49aab5c89324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461901} :answer-field/id #uuid "e21ab9c9-0c3d-5925-b233-b032c143454e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d7a83a5-f0b5-5e63-82b6-ca77f186d3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461903} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f8f614-5859-5fce-bd83-5ac2a8102396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d7a83a5-f0b5-5e63-82b6-ca77f186d3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461903} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab2eae38-ac46-5aa4-97fa-3b62105e8528" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b69e6ff7-5b7e-5a36-bad5-97913bd7c4d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120070" :question/problem "![](images/51/51273365c4a282dc3dedd9d7cd5ac7d805e1526aaeee1915e8bd95d8223c26d3.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+3x$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+x$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/a1/a14651ffc883a8c24ad17bdd031658c3d4ae21db2cfded213f2ba911fdb9a765.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=0.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=0$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↘$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+3x=x(x+3)\n$$\n\ngives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+x=x(x+1)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1$ and $x=0.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}={x}^{2}(x+3)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32b9a92b-880b-50de-b8e9-648fa219b83f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57428bd5-b536-5679-aea6-fd81151b1b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461905} {:answer/id #uuid "eca1e859-1f88-5247-ad2a-b6421e23665a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57428bd5-b536-5679-aea6-fd81151b1b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461905} :answer-field/id #uuid "32e6e343-0561-57a5-bca5-94897a041baa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e488bb-c9eb-5f1c-9403-74a0fb15149d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461907} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d9969f-476f-5ff9-80c3-e734d4ba0b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26e488bb-c9eb-5f1c-9403-74a0fb15149d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461907} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a0c5b6-3109-51ca-821e-2d69c40f39f0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1cdc35e-ec49-5951-a0f1-9d4314c0e098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461909} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e49dca-fa51-5326-9677-f3a2d54d14d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7e49dca-fa51-5326-9677-f3a2d54d14d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461910} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ba20859-bde5-5414-ae2b-f393052e586d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c84723b8-0d5e-5a26-bf52-a830d4f235da" :question/math-academy-id "q-120076" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5fdb2ddd3d07537c1e3d0d22d435928f7cd11dc7a71c67f1bf45292c82a61ef7.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x+1)$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/cf/cf2ba44d8cc21ade2204a3784af7d09b492843339a8b98c4cde741b30dfa54db.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-1.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become vertical as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x+1)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not approach $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -1.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x+1}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}=\\frac{x}{(1+\\frac{1}{x})}\\to \\pm \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become vertical as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "954f8004-35b4-58ec-be26-2beccfd5f8e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Equilibrium Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9a85761-e47d-574d-9aca-6588a7dd5c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461911} {:answer/id #uuid "25bab925-9735-5360-85d0-fde5a0511311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9a85761-e47d-574d-9aca-6588a7dd5c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461911} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd130c4-9b30-5e75-a187-0481d77ef977" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbd6c367-57f0-5f45-9efd-0993e4e7a66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461913} {:answer/id #uuid "4f892145-d69d-5017-a426-f4fbc16458ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbd6c367-57f0-5f45-9efd-0993e4e7a66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461913} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1156cf-24af-5473-8988-72a4fac212ef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eacd648-b318-52c0-a8fb-ba4fa4b7021d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461915} {:answer/id #uuid "d49308f3-03c0-5c82-91fa-efdba351adad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49308f3-03c0-5c82-91fa-efdba351adad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461916} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2fdad47-d5a7-5a45-8713-009a1d0bf9be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0faaaf1-6fed-5e12-af7b-9fca9c443b1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120109" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3d24906da8cd181d40dbaec0095b8d51481babc152609fc378b03c61187220c3.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)(y-2)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(y+1)^{2}(2-y)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/7f/7f8a042b9944b2cdf0e864b7dca760f094f4413f197befa05d6e5cbefb3841ba.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $y=-1$ and $y=2,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)(y-2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-1$ and $y=2,$ but it also evaluates to zero when $y=1,$ which is not behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=\\pm 1.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(y+1)^{2}(2-y)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-1$ and $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} {:answer/id #uuid "23c15b20-858c-5295-90c6-68f113ba9d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} :answer-field/id #uuid "52121635-762f-5923-b01d-1582f7ea794d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} {:answer/id #uuid "eba0a9bc-d740-58d4-9682-e24f2ebd01d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} :answer-field/id #uuid "b222fe66-ffd9-5e28-8684-edf53b486030" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1921f4a9-2a50-5748-bfbb-ee6ebd7a5229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461921} {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922} :answer-field/id #uuid "79c1742e-b505-51ed-b84e-0e730cf0b35e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3a19c98-b506-54b2-aa6b-86aada819468" :question/math-academy-id "q-12012" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} \\\\ 7y\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- **II.** $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- **III.** $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(kx)^{2} \\\\ 7(ky)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}({x}^{2}) \\\\ k(7y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}k({x}^{2}) \\\\ 7y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2} \\\\ 7({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+7{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ca086fd-9732-5c4b-9cb0-168433d79203" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74867da9-181e-5142-bda9-0d826272b670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461923} {:answer/id #uuid "1b78992f-e9fe-52f1-b329-9e087aa1b71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74867da9-181e-5142-bda9-0d826272b670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461923} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e21d96b-7d6c-56e5-ac65-623671510a76" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46346ac6-9690-59a2-b432-36298dc467e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461925} {:answer/id #uuid "532338a5-8803-55a0-b9a7-43ac43ec83f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "532338a5-8803-55a0-b9a7-43ac43ec83f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461926} :answer-field/id #uuid "cca5c1f4-a6cb-554d-9d1a-2a58dd0f3b9e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2803441-f1f5-5725-9ee8-efd9afb4532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461927} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1e9d88-6435-5ba7-bb92-2751d20ea073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2803441-f1f5-5725-9ee8-efd9afb4532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461927} :answer-field/id #uuid "e41132b9-d494-5928-9ebf-7b05f68c6ea3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efa92615-fa1f-50ea-a45f-eb618f2a603d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120147" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d27af23ca398eba62c2ab1fe2ee2cf9bfdf736c16fdd8408d2a13e0d34dae32c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}(2-y)$\n- ${y}^{′}=y(y-2)^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}=y(y+2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/ab/ab076b61b443e031455f07c1e976467cc3b74651bfb5fc2fb39f89a74e156681.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $y=0$ and $y=2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $y=0$ and $y=2$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $y<0$ | $0<y<2$ | $y>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}(2-y)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=0$ and $y=2,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $y<0$ | $0<y<2$ | $y>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=y(y-2)^{2}$ gives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=y(y+2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-2$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172082 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd82d96b-34d5-5d20-b810-7ea88b0b5797" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db882f9a-0289-5f76-9569-86f733e96ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461929} {:answer/id #uuid "1df5b9ec-15de-54d9-9912-26f30bd3a4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db882f9a-0289-5f76-9569-86f733e96ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461929} :answer-field/id #uuid "d28af0e5-6fb2-5c2d-9e5e-8126489054fe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d14b22ce-28bb-5e2e-97d1-bb0acb51ae7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461931} {:answer/id #uuid "fd484522-0fa7-5eeb-a1d2-a5ceba15bb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d14b22ce-28bb-5e2e-97d1-bb0acb51ae7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461931} :answer-field/id #uuid "e50ca1e1-0158-5571-bc03-0ad8b185656a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d2f3204-0315-5770-875c-0e96ce0575b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461933} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe5042f-ef3f-5b87-9a61-717250f8d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbe5042f-ef3f-5b87-9a61-717250f8d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461934} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dcc33f9-b8dc-57d3-928e-735493c6b377" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f78fc747-0bca-532e-9197-bd4cfa23233a" :question/math-academy-id "q-120228" :question/problem "![](images/20/204be6af825ef678e06526bff1fdac14ca5f09a2a7bee939620f3f2be1496985.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+3)y$\n- ${y}^{′}=(3-x)y$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/90/9051213882bcb506ddae46e0a6a79c8cd03a10eadd89e0007f895f68b00c33de.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=3$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on these lines. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- Equation I does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=3.$\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(x+3)y$ evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Equation III gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(3-x)y$ evaluates to zero at $x=3$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172018 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "244419de-9b13-5923-b0a5-1bdc6f9b03b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cabb5ac-1ea4-58ca-8ec2-a47cd57cff54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461935} {:answer/id #uuid "37d8eb56-6a47-5c3c-be71-00b9afff5a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d8eb56-6a47-5c3c-be71-00b9afff5a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461936} :answer-field/id #uuid "2044208e-d2cd-5ef8-ac7c-3b2e9445c05e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d099f48-04e6-5ec3-9d4a-22f1add13d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461937} {:answer/id #uuid "6f45a67b-6036-5ad5-acae-ada4d0516876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d099f48-04e6-5ec3-9d4a-22f1add13d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false