id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67eba06b-e142-51bc-86cf-6cd55545886d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122851" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+1},\\,3t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+1},\\,2u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{3}$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1},\\,0\\le y\\le 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d626c071-0c70-52ac-bc79-16a2a3cf5cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462085} {:answer/id #uuid "db1e1ca4-1a4a-5645-912d-ad584f2b5ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db1e1ca4-1a4a-5645-912d-ad584f2b5ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462086} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f97f6d4-1cc7-5a18-9002-6bc12e80f56c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8ec0988-8d3b-58bb-8f11-a31026537190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462087} {:answer/id #uuid "7122ea47-8dea-506b-a7e9-89375fe1971b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ec0988-8d3b-58bb-8f11-a31026537190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462087} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eccce40-3459-5071-bdd9-96e4fe102f63" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd90f72-67c5-5198-8924-c359511557f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462089} {:answer/id #uuid "97613da4-4123-53e9-ac7f-e007a645737b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97613da4-4123-53e9-ac7f-e007a645737b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462090} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e9d11d-7777-5fe2-9ce3-8596ef406783" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "261c6852-f708-5ef6-9e89-3d88f4dbba8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122868" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨2t,\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 2 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨4u,\\,2\\sqrt{2u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2k$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2x},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b20b3e-304f-5df6-8652-bce6edf26938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462091} {:answer/id #uuid "489d1517-18d2-5e62-ba9d-deff93e291da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "489d1517-18d2-5e62-ba9d-deff93e291da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462092} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa7746cf-da4e-5bea-9ac8-a9cfe214feef" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff69bf31-c057-57e2-86a4-9ee808c23372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462093} {:answer/id #uuid "91e66fa0-b75f-53ca-963d-a9fa01e18b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff69bf31-c057-57e2-86a4-9ee808c23372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462093} :answer-field/id #uuid "78ca3220-a686-585b-a4f6-89e0768fff3b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "896eb089-bc78-567d-a7b6-74bcc1d26fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462095} {:answer/id #uuid "fb746655-4225-5924-ac54-c3777ea61a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "896eb089-bc78-567d-a7b6-74bcc1d26fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462095} :answer-field/id #uuid "11fab9d7-5cc0-5afc-bb7d-b8c6c494f124" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e297ed2-2489-5ad9-8dda-10806650784e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122935" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-10,-2]?$\n- **I.** ${-10,-9,-8,-4,-2}$\n- **II.** ${-9,-5,-4,-2}$\n- **III.** $-10<-6<-4<-3$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-10,-2].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-10,-2]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-10.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[-10,-2]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26715d5c-8967-5870-a32d-f0e7de04504e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462097} {:answer/id #uuid "cffe34d1-2420-5409-9740-ce2cb5bd06e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26715d5c-8967-5870-a32d-f0e7de04504e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462097} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a63827-ba0c-5262-83e4-7514a1d6d98a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5500db0b-5028-5ca1-9101-be045fa07fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462099} {:answer/id #uuid "f59f0c27-693f-5b74-9c2c-1f1aaecba22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5500db0b-5028-5ca1-9101-be045fa07fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462099} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bd4fdc7-a23b-54cd-bd68-59ae2ea9f1c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462803} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfc8220c-0f8b-58d7-84b9-a08eddb6eba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462101} {:answer/id #uuid "646e11a8-a44c-5fe3-934b-ea14c43adefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646e11a8-a44c-5fe3-934b-ea14c43adefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462102} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e42328f-21c1-5e9f-b9f3-96c9ef90effe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bede805a-096d-538b-aca7-d4841b6beb80" :question/math-academy-id "q-122937" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-3,7]?$\n- **I.** ${-3,-5,1,2,6}$\n- **II.** ${-3,0,3,7,8}$\n- **III.** ${-3,-2,1,3,4,7}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=7.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[-3,7].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[-3,7].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title 